<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Algirdas Brazauskas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1932–2010</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algirdas">Algirdas</a> Brazauskas was a Lithuanian politician who became first secretary of the Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> in 1988 and in 1989 led it to break away from the Soviet party, backing the independence movement. After independence he served as president from 1993 to 1998 and as prime minister from 2001 to 2006.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/algirdas-brazauskas.jpg" alt="Algirdas Brazauskas" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Magnus Fröderberg · CC BY 2.5 dk · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Algirdas_Mykkolas_Brazauskas,_Litauens_statsminster,_under_det_Nordiskt-Baltiska_statsministermotet_i_Reykjavik_2005-10-24.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
